      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i noticed you called some objections \"dangerous misconceptions\" and said scientists frame them that way—it sounds like you're saying the scientific side pretty much has the moral high ground here since they're looking at the \"social contract\" and \"national well-being\" while the other side is just \"hyper-individualistic.\" \n\nif i'm writing this op-ed, shouldn't i present the civil liberties side as having a legitimate moral framework too, or is it actually more accurate to say their arguments are logically inconsistent with modern public health needs?",
